@copilot Agreed on the diagnosis — your second review reached the same conclusion I did ("*fix the generator/template ... then regenerate*"), so we're aligned. I've now traced it to the exact emitters and recorded them on `xboing-qspw`:

**Defect 1 — reporting line, two vocabularies, same file:**

```go
// internal/hook/generate_agents.go:445  -> identity form, "Claude Agento (claude)"
return fmt.Sprintf("You report to %s.", joinWithOxford(names))

// internal/hook/generate_agents.go:727  -> role-slug form, "coo" / "vision-keeper"
fmt.Fprintf(&b, "You report to %s. These are not yours:\n\n", joinWithOxford(targets))
```

There's a third renderer at `internal/hook/subagent_start.go:864`, so the sentence is spelled three times across two files. That's the root cause — no single helper owns how a reporting relationship is written.

**Defect 2 — the comma splice, also duplicated:**

```go
// internal/hook/generate_agents.go:670
fmt.Fprintf(&b, "\nYou are %s (%s), %s.\n", id.Name, id.Handle, firstLine)
// internal/hook/persona.go:42
fmt.Fprintf(&b, "You are %s (%s), %s.", id.Name, id.Handle, first)
```

Plus the tests that pin the current strings: `subagent_start_test.go:117`, `:1133`, `subprocess_test.go:617`.

**On your alternative — "or excluded from this PR":** I'm keeping the file in. Excluding it doesn't make the regeneration go away; it leaves it dirty in the working tree to be re-discovered every session. The artifact here is *correct output of a flawed template*, and it matches the four sibling files already on `master`. Committing it keeps the five consistent; the template fix will regenerate all five together.

Both findings are recorded, located, and actionable upstream. Nothing further to change in this repo, so I'm merging.
